Say how long each GPU-side stage of drawing takes, on OHOS.

HDR 1080p60 video (VP9 profile 2, decoded in software) dropped about a third
of its frames on a Mate 70 Pro+ in the default power mode, SDR 1080p60 none.
ohos-video-submit-diagnostics.patch put the drops on viz's acknowledgement
of each video frame: 5-7 ms for HDR against about 1 ms for SDR. Leaving the
native window untagged, so the system composites it as SDR, halved the
drops; this times the half that is Chromium's.

On OHOS each of these logs, every 300 calls ("OHOS gpu stage"), its average
and longest time and how many calls took over 8 ms:
- WritePixelsYUV: RasterDecoderImpl::DoWritePixelsYUVINTERNAL, which writes
  a software-decoded frame's planes into its shared image (half-float
  planes for 10-bit video);
- viz DrawAndSwap: Display::DrawAndSwap on viz's compositor thread;
- FinishPaintCurrentFrame and SwapBuffers: SkiaOutputSurfaceImplOnGpu on
  the GPU thread, which replay and submit the frame and present it.

Generated against Chromium 154.0.8037.51.

Apply with:
  git -C /path/to/chromium/src apply /path/to/patches/ohos-gpu-stage-diagnostics.patch

